todd phillips the director of the  upcoming joker movie has publicly  revealed the first official look at  joaquin phoenix in the lead role the  surprisingly stripped-down image was  posted to philip's instagram page with a  one-word caption  arthur without the context of the  upcoming solo movie you'd never know  this was supposed to be a portrait of  the clown prince of crime  saved for a greasy hairstyle and a few  extra wrinkles  phoenix looks a lot like himself in the  photo but there's a reason for that  phillips who has directed films like old  school starsky and hutch and the three  movies of the hangover series  isn't making a movie about the joker at  the height of his powers instead  joker is expected to be a dark and  experimental story  reportedly centering around a failed  comedian in the 1980s who snaps and  transitions to a legendary life of crime  phoenix is playing the joker as an  everyday guy and this glimpse appears to  be from just before one of his bad days  sends him over the edge  with that in mind it makes sense that  the first reveal of phoenix in character  doesn't feature him in the typical joker  look here he's just a fairly normal dude  struggling to realize his dream of  making people laugh when he comes to  terms with the fact that his career may  never take off  he takes matters into his own hands in a  decidedly theatrical way  it sounds pretty relatable aside from  the whole domestic terrorism thing  phillips's big reveal seems to confirm a  previous report by that hashtag show  that stirred up a ton of hype  in july the outlet posted an article  claiming that the joker's real name in  the movie would be revealed as arthur  fleck  now that phillips himself has mentioned  the name it seems a sure bet that mr  fleck is our leading man  in the same write-up that hashtag show  also reported that the joker movie will  see arthur moving in with his sick  mother  penny and later meeting a woman named  sophie dumond who may be played by zazie  beats of atlanta and deadpool 2.  other reports would seem to corroborate  those details the outlet's most  outlandish hypothesis that the joker and  the batman will be revealed to be half  brothers has yet to be confirmed or  denied but we do know that batman's  father  thomas wayne will be a part of the movie  so perhaps there's some truth to that  tidbit  as well a major part of the joker's  appeal over the years has been his  generally unknown constantly shifting  origins aside from the 1989 batman movie  which presented the character as a  gangster named  jack napier the joker typically hasn't  been shown as having a traditional  backstory he's usually more of an agent  of chaos with a contradictory history  that he routinely lies about  you wanna know how i got these scars  despite that history of ambiguity the  fact that this movie appears to be  nailing down  one origin story for the joker isn't  anything to be alarmed about  it's not meant to be a definitive  interpretation just a different one  the fox series gotham a prequel of sorts  to the world of batman  has also spent the last few years  playing around with the joker inspired  characters  jerome and jeremiah veleska unhinged  villains who have frequently been teased  as potentially being younger versions of  the joker we know  but what's true in the world of gotham  doesn't need to be true for any other  batman story  and the same goes for this solo movie  unlike the shared universe occupied by  movies like suicide squad  wonder woman and justice league joaquin  phoenix's joker movie is set to be a  standalone film  existing outside of established  continuity to tell a radically different  story it's a new approach for dc comics  on screen  and if it works out we can probably  expect other alternate universe else  worlds type stories to follow like the  soviet union superman story  superman red sun this alternate universe  aspect is a big part of what makes  joker so potentially special it gives  phillips and phoenix the freedom to be  weird and takes chances without worrying  about sequels spin-offs or what's going  on in the batman movies  it's a great first look at one of 2019's  most curious projects  and we can't wait to find out more  you just couldn't let me go could you
 

